## What I did

**Bug found in `src/commands_retry.rs`:** `extract_tool_name_from_error` (used by `/retry` to give tool-specific recovery hints) only checked the *first* occurrence of each tool name in the error string. If that first occurrence was embedded inside another word (e.g. `"bashful"`), it was rejected — but the loop moved on, never checking later standalone occurrences. So an error like `"bashful shell: bash exited with code 1"` returned None instead of `Some("bash")`, silently dropping the recovery hint.

**Fix:** iterate over all occurrences of each tool name per the word-boundary rules, advancing past non-matching occurrences. The earliest standalone match wins (preserving the existing longest-first tool ordering).

**Process:**
• Wrote 3 regression tests first (`plain, embedded`, `embedded-first-occurrence`) — the last one failed, confirming the bug
• Fixed with a small surgical edit; ran full gates
• `cargo fmt, cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings, cargo build, and cargo test` (4315 + 88 pass) all green

Committed immediately as a single small improvement per the fallback-task rules. No docs change needed — this is an internal helper fix with no user-facing surface change.
